<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- ============================================================
     PiBoard - build/entitlements.mac.plist
     Entitlements du "hardened runtime", requis par la notarisation
     Apple depuis la 1.139.3 (voir electron-builder.yml). Ce ne sont
     PAS des permissions App Sandbox (PiBoard n'est pas distribue par
     le Mac App Store, donc pas sandboxe) : ce sont des EXCEPTIONS aux
     protections par defaut du hardened runtime, sans lesquelles
     Electron lui-meme (V8/JIT) crashe au lancement sur une
     application signee.

     Les binaires systeme que PiBoard lance en processus enfant (ping,
     arp, dscacheutil, netstat, scutil, curl, ditto, vm_stat...) ne
     sont pas concernes par ce fichier : le hardened runtime ne
     restreint pas le lancement d'autres programmes, seulement ce que
     le processus de PiBoard fait lui-meme en memoire. Ce qui regit
     ces appels-la, c'est l'autorisation systeme "Reseau local" (voir
     docs/LINUX-MACOS.md et le widget Analyse reseau) — separee de
     la signature, meme si une signature stable est ce qui lui permet
     desormais de persister correctement d'une mise a jour a l'autre.

     Hardened runtime entitlements, required by Apple notarization
     since 1.139.3 (see electron-builder.yml). These are NOT App
     Sandbox permissions (PiBoard is not distributed through the Mac
     App Store, so it is not sandboxed): they are EXCEPTIONS to the
     hardened runtime's default protections, without which Electron
     itself (V8/JIT) crashes on launch once the app is signed.

     The system binaries PiBoard runs as child processes (ping, arp,
     dscacheutil, netstat, scutil, curl, ditto, vm_stat...) are
     unaffected by this file: hardened runtime does not restrict
     launching other programs, only what PiBoard's own process does in
     memory. What governs those calls is the system's "Local Network"
     permission (see docs/LINUX-MACOS.md and the Network scan widget)
     — separate from signing, even though a stable signature is what
     now lets it persist correctly across updates.
     ============================================================ -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- Requis par V8 (le moteur JavaScript de Chromium/Node) pour
       generer du code executable a la volee. Sans cette entree,
       Electron crashe immediatement au lancement sous hardened
       runtime, sur TOUTE application Electron, pas seulement PiBoard.
       Required by V8 (Chromium/Node's JavaScript engine) to generate
       executable code on the fly. Without this entry, Electron
       crashes immediately on launch under hardened runtime, on ANY
       Electron app, not just PiBoard. -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
  <true/>

  <!-- Meme besoin que ci-dessus pour certaines zones memoire de V8 non
       couvertes par allow-jit seul.
       Same need as above, for some V8 memory regions not covered by
       allow-jit alone. -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
  <true/>

  <!-- Electron lit des variables DYLD_* pour charger certains de ses
       composants internes (notamment en developpement local via
       `npm run electron`) ; le hardened runtime les bloque sinon.
       Electron reads DYLD_* variables to load some of its internal
       components (notably in local development via `npm run
       electron`); hardened runtime blocks them otherwise. -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables</key>
  <true/>

  <!-- PiBoard n'embarque aucun module natif aujourd'hui, mais
       Electron lui-meme charge des frameworks non signes par Apple
       (ses propres .framework). Sans cette entree, le chargement
       echoue sous hardened runtime.
       PiBoard embeds no native module today, but Electron itself
       loads frameworks not signed by Apple (its own .framework
       bundles). Without this entry, loading fails under hardened
       runtime. -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
